{
  "about": "B-2c (24 Nov 2026): Praveen's Master BOQ Excel formulas (Master_BOQ.xlsx, Sheet1, column E) as BOQ formula rules, with only his ruled corrections: the 10 kW inverter counts in every per-inverter rule (F4-14); R20 counts DCDBs and every ACDB (F4-15); the 100 mm fittings come from the 100 mm pipe (G2); packs, pieces and metres round up (F4-17); at least 1 only when the drivers are above 0 (G3). THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH: load_formula_rules --apply makes the active rules match it, including switching back on a rule switched off with --deactivate. R24 and R25 are loaded switched off (active false) until the Tin Shade and Ballast lines are re-counted in Nos (fix_tin_shade_ballast --apply-counts); set them to true and --apply again then.",
